    1. Pick grid 15x15, choose 3 distinct colors for bg, fill, marker.
    2. Choose N=4-6 rectangles with random dims (h,w in 2-7 each).
    3. Place rectangles on grid with >=1 pixel gap between all pairs and bg remaining one connected component. Use rejection or greedy packing.
    4. For each rect, scatter marker pixels randomly (density 4-33%, at least 1).
    5. Assign marker counts ensuring exactly one rect has a unique minimum count. Pick the target rect first, give it k markers, then give all others >k markers.
    6. Fill remaining rect cells with fill color, remaining grid cells with bg.
    7. Verify bg is one 4-connected component and marker total < fill total.
